00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:02.149 align:start position:0%
 
bungie is coming up on its 30th  anniversary and the developer has all  the momentum in the world dropping the  dopest reveal for destiny 2 the witch  queen and kicking off the annual hype  cycle once more if you're into destiny  or all things gaming be sure to drop a  like and sub to this channel as well but  before we start i want to quickly  mention one thing if your opinion of  destiny 2 is based on the game from  prior years honestly just save yourself  some time this video isn't really for  those who want to just stop by and tell  me that the game is dead it's got over  20 million new players we're having a  blast with some of the best storytelling  in world building in years and bungie  has shown no signs of stopping or  catering to the folks that have no  intention of playing so do me a solid  stop it  get some help now if you're like us and  you're excited for this expansion then  all i can say is welcome and let's dive  into everything you need to know about  destiny 2 the witch queen  to start it off we have to talk about  the witch queen herself savathune is one  of the primary antagonists of the  destiny universe but so far we've only  dealt with her brother oryx during the  taken king expansion and her sister sivu  arath during this season of the hunt  savathun is more cunning than her  siblings and has been pulling plenty of  strings behind the scenes from  evaluating our capabilities as guardians  during the season of the splicer to  taking riven the last amkara and  unleashing a curse cycle upon the  dreaming city now she's out in full  force welcoming us to her throne world  and daring us to survive the truth but  what does that mean  the truth in the witch queen expansion  seems to be that savathun has been  gifted the light giving the hive brand  new powers on par with guardians and it  is a sight to behold as we face  salvathun's loosened brood hundreds of  hypestyle ghosts frantically search the  battlefield reviving fallen hive  combatants and resurrecting them with  terrifying new powers many of which look  like our own but are now being wielded  against us there is one distinct feature  that separates the hive ghosts and it's  the fact that it doesn't quite look like  their powers of the light are one-to-one  with the guardians guardians get their  light from the traveler's ghost and  savathun is notorious for being cunning  and a trickster of sorts which leads me  to believe that the powers of light that  are granted to our enemies are merely  some kind of illusion or trick of being  in her throne world on bungie's launch  page for the witch queen the developer  alludes to this with the section  covering some of the new activities  labeled solve the mystery pierce the lie  a lot of the teasers leading up to the  reveal of the witch queen were also  framed with quote survive the truth  which supports the idea that what we're  seeing from savathun is just another one  of her intricate webs of lies and  deception and that we'll be spending  most of our time trying to lift that  veil so beyond the campaign the witch  queen will be chock full of different  content like a new six player match made  activity at the heart of the throne  world details are slim at the moment but  there's mention of balance needing to be  maintained each season so far this past  year has had some kind of a six player  match made activity such as season of  the splicers override and they all play  with similar themes of guardians  basically playing the role of  maintenance and keeping the environment  balanced or progressively inching closer  towards an ultimate goal for the season  finale there will also be a new raid and  more raids and dungeons to look forward  to post-witch queen as well raids have  been pretty dry this past year with only  two raids released in over a year and a  half which is quite the drought for some  of destiny's best and most memorable  endgame content so far we had the deep  stone crypt last year with beyond lights  launch and the reprised vault of glass  and season of the splicer but this time  around we're getting a brand new raid in  the witch queen the raid takes place in  the swamps of savathun's throne world  and lies in a sunken pyramid some of you  may already know the pyramids are kind  of the symbol for the darkness and we've  traveled inside one of them before  during shadow keep i am so excited and i  can't wait to see how a raid inside one  of these massive ships will be  especially inside savathun's throne  world it's also been confirmed that  older raids will be reprised and  returning so there will be more raids in  the near future which is great news now  the jury is out on whether older raids  from destiny 1 like crota's end will get  the remaster treatment or if bungie  simply plans on cycling out raids like  the last wish to make room for something  from their destiny content vault like  the leviathan personally in regards to  the destiny 1 raids coming back i get  tired of revamped content pretty quickly  despite enjoying the nostalgia at first  but there are millions of destiny 2  players that have never seen this  content so i have no issue with more  reprised raids to help stem the content  drought between seasons we've covered a  good chunk of news so far but let's  shift gears towards some of the other  types of content and gameplay changes  for starters the witch queen has a  difficulty modifier on its campaign you  can try to sweat it out on legendary  mode which means you can earn even more  powerful gear and extra rewards there's  also weapon crafting a first for destiny  there's an argument to be made that the  current umbral engram system could  qualify as a sort of crafting but that  is really kind of its own thing in my  book with umbrals you can invest certain  materials to try to dodge the rng of the  game a little bit by curating your loot  drops you can make an engram for example  drop a piece of armor with a high  mobility stat but you're still not sure  what kind of armor piece you're gonna  get or from what set but you're banking  on the mobility stat being decent enough  to potentially rotate into your armor  lineup with weapon crafting and the  witch queen it seems like we're taking  things a step further by being able to  craft all witch queen and seasonal  weapons and even trying hunting for  specific perks to craft with crafting  there's also the brand new glaive  destiny's first and only first person  melee weapon the glaive is a versatile  new energy weapon archetype that lets  you use melee combos mid-range  projectiles and defensive capabilities i  won't even lie to you it looks sick as  [ __ ] and i'm excited to see the class  specific exotic variants with all this  dope new content to look forward to it  begs the question for destiny 2 fans  which version of the witch queen should  you get to briefly summarize you have a  standard edition a deluxe edition and a  pricey collector's editions which at the  time of this video is actually already  sold out so  they all kind of speak for themselves if  you're a casual or new player and you're  unsure if you want to stick with destiny  throughout the year then the standard  edition is for you it's a fairly  complete experience with all of the  witch queen's content but it doesn't  come with the seasonal activities the  deluxe edition is your best bet as  there's plenty of seasonal content worth  diving into like dungeons exotic weapons  and other bits of content the  collector's edition is obviously for  fanatics like our very own phil hornshaw  who knows every little thing there is to  know about the lore and has some wicked  good lore articles for newcomers and  veterans alike destiny 2 the witch queen  is basically on the same tier as the big  fall expansions of the past despite  having a february 2022 release date  before the bungie activision split the  taken king and forsaken were massive  content drops after bungie went  independent their large fall expansions  like shadow keep and beyond light were  hefty but not nearly as grand relying  upon the seasonal content and season  pass to kind of help pad the stats a  little bit so to speak that being said  though all the expansions were an  absolute must play that first month and  ever since bungie moved on from the  stale and monotonous small scale dlc  like curse of osiris and warmind they  have found better ways to keep the  content fresh on a regular cadence even  though it might still be a bit of a drip  feed for the hardcore players who pump  dozens of hours a month to where they're  spending the majority of their time  trying to like solo or two-man  encounters that usually have six players  it's also worth mentioning that pvp  deserves more love and although there  have been great threats from the  developers talking about focusing on pvp  post witch queen there are obviously  things to be wary about but where's the  fun complaining about all that man it's  [ __ ] destiny we're getting a new drop  in february with brand new weapons sick  ass armor new raids new activities new  story new everything i'm so excited to  kick some hive ass and i hope you're  down to come along for the ride too  until next time  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  you

